				\setlength{\oddsidemargin}{-69pt}
				\begin{document}$${D}_{T} \ge {\overline {X}}+2\delta$$\end{document}DT≥X¯+2δDT is the docking threshold, X̄ is the average TPSS of the entire Library (1 or 2) solutions; and δ is the TPSS standard deviation of the entire Library (1 or 2) solutions.

Molecular docking solutions from both libraries 1 and 2 were rescored by calculating their binding free energies (ΔGBind). Two docking postprocessing strategies were implemented. Strategy A: excluding phospholipids neighboring the pore, and strategy B: including key phospholipids neighboring the pore that could influence small molecule binding. ΔGBind calculations were carried out using MM-GBSA methods86 with Prime162, combining molecular mechanics energies and implicit solvation models163. The MM-GBSA ΔGBind between ligands and the TMC1 channel was calculated with the following equations:2\documentclass[12pt]{minimal}
